# Build context for src/Api/Dockerfile, which is the repository root so that Directory.Build.props
# and Directory.Packages.props are available at restore time.
#
# This file did not exist until 2026-08-25, and its absence was not merely slow — it was a
# correctness bug. `COPY src/ src/` copied the HOST's bin/ and obj/ into the image, overwriting the
# restore output produced by the layer above with a project.assets.json full of Windows paths. The
# publish then failed with NETSDK1064 "Package Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi ... was not found",
# which reads like a NuGet problem and is not one.
#
# It also cut the context from 522 MB to a few megabytes.

# Build output — the image builds its own.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
src/Web/dist/
web-dist/

# Version control and tooling.
.git/
.github/
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Test and local artefacts.
TestResults/
**/*.trx
shots/
*.log

# Local secrets and overrides. Nothing here should ever reach an image.
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/appsettings.*.Local.json
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Documentation and process. None of it is needed to compile the API, and excluding it keeps a
# rebuild off the critical path when only a story or a decision changes.
*.md
docs/
meetings/
proposals/
qa/
stories/
ux/
process/
deploy/
.claude/
